<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas III of Saluzzo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1356–<a href="/years/1416">1416</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Tommaso III of Saluzzo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas III was Marquis of Saluzzo from 1396 to 1416. Captured in 1394 during wars with the princes of Savoy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, he spent his imprisonment in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> writing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-chevalier-errant">Le Chevalier errant</a>, an allegorical romance in French. He spent long periods at the French court and defended Saluzzo's independence from Savoy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-iii-of-saluzzo.jpg" alt="Thomas III of Saluzzo" width="320" height="708" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_III_of_Saluzzo_as_Alexander_the_Great.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
